WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.102
Separate pronouns. Twelve
words you will see every day.

2
00:00:04.452 --> 00:00:06.330
Stage three is about fixed words.

3
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:10.195
We start with the pronouns. I,
he, she, we, and their friends.

4
00:00:10.845 --> 00:00:13.260
Chapter one. Why we learn fixed words now.

5
00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.079
Fixed words are in almost every sentence.

6
00:00:16.229 --> 00:00:20.708
Pronouns are fixed words. So are
pointing words, like the word for this.

7
00:00:20.958 --> 00:00:21.674
‫هَذَا‬

8
00:00:22.024 --> 00:00:25.174
And so are question words.
They come again and again.

9
00:00:25.524 --> 00:00:27.088
Their ending never changes.

10
00:00:27.238 --> 00:00:31.536
So you learn each one once, as a word
in a table. Then you know it for good.

11
00:00:31.886 --> 00:00:34.572
When you know them, every
later example is easier.

12
00:00:34.722 --> 00:00:38.939
You see the fixed words at once. Then
you look only at the flexible ones.

13
00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:40.646
Here are four pronouns.

14
00:00:40.896 --> 00:00:41.509
I.

15
00:00:41.659 --> 00:00:42.492
‫أَنَا‬

16
00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:43.595
He, or it.

17
00:00:43.745 --> 00:00:44.566
‫هُوَ‬

18
00:00:44.916 --> 00:00:45.683
She, or it.

19
00:00:45.833 --> 00:00:46.514
‫هِيَ‬

20
00:00:46.864 --> 00:00:47.476
We.

21
00:00:47.626 --> 00:00:48.471
‫نَحْنُ‬

22
00:00:49.121 --> 00:00:52.278
Chapter two. Fixed and
flexible. A quick recap.

23
00:00:52.728 --> 00:00:55.021
Every word is either fixed or flexible.

24
00:00:55.271 --> 00:00:56.629
First, a fixed word.

25
00:00:56.779 --> 00:00:57.799
‫مَبْنِيٌّ‬

26
00:00:58.149 --> 00:00:59.741
Its ending never changes.

27
00:00:59.891 --> 00:01:03.607
The word for he never changes.
It is the same in every sentence.

28
00:01:03.857 --> 00:01:04.678
‫هُوَ‬

29
00:01:05.128 --> 00:01:06.497
Then, a flexible word.

30
00:01:06.647 --> 00:01:07.655
‫مُعْرَبٌ‬

31
00:01:08.005 --> 00:01:09.676
Its ending changes with the job.

32
00:01:09.826 --> 00:01:11.150
The house, with damma.

33
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.218
‫البَيْتُ‬

34
00:01:12.568 --> 00:01:14.576
And after a preposition, with kasra.

35
00:01:14.726 --> 00:01:15.684
‫البَيْتِ‬

36
00:01:16.134 --> 00:01:20.024
Pronouns are fixed. Their ending
stays the same, whatever the job.

37
00:01:22.367 --> 00:01:24.937
Chapter three. The
twelve separate pronouns.

38
00:01:25.387 --> 00:01:26.929
Learn this table by heart.

39
00:01:27.029 --> 00:01:30.270
Read it aloud, top to
bottom, every day this week.

40
00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.646
Each row gives the person,
the number and the gender.

41
00:01:33.646 --> 00:01:35.592
Then the Arabic, and its meaning.

42
00:01:35.942 --> 00:01:39.519
First person, the speaker
alone. A man or a woman. I.

43
00:01:39.669 --> 00:01:40.502
‫أَنَا‬

44
00:01:40.852 --> 00:01:44.255
The speaker with others. Two
or more, men or women. We.

45
00:01:44.405 --> 00:01:45.250
‫نَحْنُ‬

46
00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.450
Second person, the listener. One man. You.

47
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:49.429
‫أَنْتَ‬

48
00:01:49.779 --> 00:01:51.795
Second person, one woman. You.

49
00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:52.804
‫أَنْتِ‬

50
00:01:53.154 --> 00:01:56.124
Second person, two people,
men or women. You two.

51
00:01:56.274 --> 00:01:57.281
‫أَنْتُمَا‬

52
00:01:57.631 --> 00:02:01.306
Second person, three or more.
Men, or men and women. You.

53
00:02:01.456 --> 00:02:02.428
‫أَنْتُمْ‬

54
00:02:02.778 --> 00:02:05.151
Second person, three or more women. You.

55
00:02:05.301 --> 00:02:06.555
‫أَنْتُنَّ‬

56
00:02:06.905 --> 00:02:10.479
Third person, the absent one.
One, masculine. He, or it.

57
00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:11.450
‫هُوَ‬

58
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:14.166
Third person, one, feminine. She, or it.

59
00:02:14.316 --> 00:02:14.997
‫هِيَ‬

60
00:02:15.347 --> 00:02:18.984
Third person, two people, men
or women. They, the two of them.

61
00:02:19.134 --> 00:02:19.925
‫هُمَا‬

62
00:02:20.275 --> 00:02:23.957
Third person, three or more.
Men, or men and women. They.

63
00:02:24.107 --> 00:02:24.819
‫هُمْ‬

64
00:02:25.169 --> 00:02:27.475
Third person, three or more women. They.

65
00:02:27.625 --> 00:02:28.453
‫هُنَّ‬

66
00:02:29.103 --> 00:02:31.437
That is the whole table. Twelve words.

67
00:02:32.087 --> 00:02:34.139
A tip. Watch the small vowels.

68
00:02:34.389 --> 00:02:36.519
For one man, fatha on the last letter.

69
00:02:36.669 --> 00:02:37.498
‫أَنْتَ‬

70
00:02:37.848 --> 00:02:40.151
For one woman, kasra on the last letter.

71
00:02:40.301 --> 00:02:41.160
‫أَنْتِ‬

72
00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:44.797
For a group of men, the last
letter is an m, with sukūn.

73
00:02:44.947 --> 00:02:45.659
‫هُمْ‬

74
00:02:46.009 --> 00:02:49.416
For a group of women, the last
letter is an n, with a shadda.

75
00:02:49.566 --> 00:02:50.394
‫هُنَّ‬

76
00:02:50.744 --> 00:02:53.801
A small mark, or one
letter, changes the meaning.

77
00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:56.109
So read every letter and every vowel.

78
00:02:56.759 --> 00:02:59.998
A side note. Each pronoun
is built on one fixed mark.

79
00:03:00.248 --> 00:03:01.069
‫هُوَ‬

80
00:03:01.319 --> 00:03:02.318
Built on fatha.

81
00:03:02.468 --> 00:03:03.313
‫نَحْنُ‬

82
00:03:03.563 --> 00:03:04.389
On damma.

83
00:03:04.539 --> 00:03:05.251
‫هُمْ‬

84
00:03:05.501 --> 00:03:06.409
On sukūn.

85
00:03:06.659 --> 00:03:08.219
You do not need to learn these.

86
00:03:08.369 --> 00:03:10.395
Just remember the word never changes.

87
00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.594
Chapter four. Three groups.

88
00:03:15.044 --> 00:03:17.840
The twelve pronouns
fall into three groups.

89
00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.026
Each group is one person:
first, second or third.

90
00:03:21.276 --> 00:03:22.837
First person is the speaker.

91
00:03:22.987 --> 00:03:24.378
‫المُتَكَلِّمُ‬

92
00:03:24.728 --> 00:03:26.262
Two words. I, and we.

93
00:03:26.412 --> 00:03:27.245
‫أَنَا‬

94
00:03:27.395 --> 00:03:28.240
‫نَحْنُ‬

95
00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:31.751
Second person is the
listener. The one you talk to.

96
00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:33.123
‫المُخَاطَبُ‬

97
00:03:33.473 --> 00:03:35.938
Five words. They all begin the same way.

98
00:03:36.088 --> 00:03:36.917
‫أَنْتَ‬

99
00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:37.926
‫أَنْتِ‬

100
00:03:38.076 --> 00:03:39.083
‫أَنْتُمَا‬

101
00:03:39.233 --> 00:03:40.205
‫أَنْتُمْ‬

102
00:03:40.355 --> 00:03:41.609
‫أَنْتُنَّ‬

103
00:03:42.059 --> 00:03:45.203
Third person is the absent
one. The one you talk about.

104
00:03:45.353 --> 00:03:46.561
‫الغَائِبُ‬

105
00:03:46.911 --> 00:03:48.187
Five words again.

106
00:03:48.337 --> 00:03:49.158
‫هُوَ‬

107
00:03:49.308 --> 00:03:49.989
‫هِيَ‬

108
00:03:50.139 --> 00:03:50.930
‫هُمَا‬

109
00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:51.792
‫هُمْ‬

110
00:03:51.942 --> 00:03:52.770
‫هُنَّ‬

111
00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.346
Two, five and five. Twelve in all.

112
00:03:55.996 --> 00:03:57.920
A tip about the words for he and she.

113
00:03:58.170 --> 00:03:58.991
‫هُوَ‬

114
00:03:59.141 --> 00:03:59.822
‫هِيَ‬

115
00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:01.715
They are also used for things.

116
00:04:01.965 --> 00:04:03.610
For a masculine noun, use

117
00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:04.481
‫هُوَ‬

118
00:04:04.731 --> 00:04:06.338
For a feminine noun, use

119
00:04:06.388 --> 00:04:07.069
‫هِيَ‬

120
00:04:07.419 --> 00:04:10.579
For example. Where is the
watch? It is on the bed.

121
00:04:10.829 --> 00:04:14.756
‫أَيْنَ السَّاعَةُ؟ هِيَ عَلَى السَّرِيرِ‬

122
00:04:15.106 --> 00:04:18.472
The watch is a feminine noun.
So we use the word for she.

123
00:04:19.122 --> 00:04:24.140
Another tip. For two people, there is
one word. Men or women, it is the same.

124
00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.715
Talking to two people.

125
00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:26.872
‫أَنْتُمَا‬

126
00:04:27.222 --> 00:04:28.564
Talking about two people.

127
00:04:28.714 --> 00:04:29.505
‫هُمَا‬

128
00:04:29.855 --> 00:04:32.667
For a group of men and women
together, talking to them.

129
00:04:32.817 --> 00:04:33.789
‫أَنْتُمْ‬

130
00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:35.316
Talking about them.

131
00:04:35.466 --> 00:04:36.178
‫هُمْ‬

132
00:04:38.534 --> 00:04:41.190
Chapter five. A fixed
word still has a job.

133
00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.798
A pronoun never changes its last vowel.

134
00:04:43.948 --> 00:04:46.362
Its ending cannot show rafʿ, naṣb or jarr.

135
00:04:46.512 --> 00:04:49.481
But it still does a job in
the sentence, like any noun.

136
00:04:49.931 --> 00:04:51.956
Here is the rule. The place of rafʿ.

137
00:04:52.206 --> 00:04:54.379
Look at this sentence. He is a student.

138
00:04:54.529 --> 00:04:55.943
‫هُوَ طَالِبٌ‬

139
00:04:56.293 --> 00:04:57.898
The word for he is the Topic.

140
00:04:58.048 --> 00:04:59.217
A Topic is rafʿ.

141
00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:02.702
But this word cannot show a
damma. Its ending is fixed.

142
00:05:02.952 --> 00:05:04.923
So we say it is in the place of rafʿ.

143
00:05:05.173 --> 00:05:07.513
‫فِي مَحَلِّ رَفْعٍ‬

144
00:05:07.863 --> 00:05:11.714
The ending shows no sign. But the
job still gives the word its place.

145
00:05:12.364 --> 00:05:14.745
So we describe a fixed word in two steps.

146
00:05:14.895 --> 00:05:16.968
First its job. Then its place.

147
00:05:17.318 --> 00:05:19.716
Here is our sentence again, word by word.

148
00:05:19.966 --> 00:05:20.927
The first word.

149
00:05:21.077 --> 00:05:21.898
‫هُوَ‬

150
00:05:22.248 --> 00:05:26.154
Its job is the Topic. Its ending
is fixed. It never changes.

151
00:05:26.304 --> 00:05:27.843
So it is in the place of rafʿ.

152
00:05:28.293 --> 00:05:29.278
The second word.

153
00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:30.413
‫طَالِبٌ‬

154
00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:35.434
Its job is the Information. It ends
in tanween damma, and you can see it.

155
00:05:35.584 --> 00:05:36.902
So it is simply rafʿ.

156
00:05:37.252 --> 00:05:41.161
Both words are rafʿ. The
Information shows it on its ending.

157
00:05:41.161 --> 00:05:43.442
The Topic has it only in its place.

158
00:05:44.092 --> 00:05:46.336
Good to know. There are three places.

159
00:05:46.586 --> 00:05:48.926
‫فِي مَحَلِّ رَفْعٍ‬

160
00:05:49.076 --> 00:05:50.170
The place of rafʿ.

161
00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.563
‫فِي مَحَلِّ نَصْبٍ‬

162
00:05:52.713 --> 00:05:53.899
The place of naṣb.

163
00:05:54.149 --> 00:05:56.270
‫فِي مَحَلِّ جَرٍّ‬

164
00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:57.496
The place of jarr.

165
00:05:57.846 --> 00:06:01.529
In this stage, these twelve pronouns
are always in the place of rafʿ.

166
00:06:03.867 --> 00:06:06.248
Chapter six. Sentences with a pronoun.

167
00:06:06.698 --> 00:06:08.259
Here the pronoun is the Topic.

168
00:06:08.409 --> 00:06:11.721
The Information is a noun, or
a phrase that tells you where.

169
00:06:12.171 --> 00:06:13.671
One. I am a student.

170
00:06:13.821 --> 00:06:15.428
‫أَنَا طَالِبٌ‬

171
00:06:15.778 --> 00:06:18.309
The word for I is the
Topic, in the place of rafʿ.

172
00:06:18.459 --> 00:06:22.073
Student is the Information. It
is rafʿ, with tanween damma.

173
00:06:22.523 --> 00:06:24.146
Two. She is a teacher.

174
00:06:24.296 --> 00:06:25.737
‫هِيَ مُدَرِّسَةٌ‬

175
00:06:26.087 --> 00:06:28.755
The word for she is the
Topic, in the place of rafʿ.

176
00:06:29.205 --> 00:06:31.038
Three. We are in the classroom.

177
00:06:31.188 --> 00:06:33.166
‫نَحْنُ فِي الفَصْلِ‬

178
00:06:33.516 --> 00:06:36.208
The word for we is the
Topic, in the place of rafʿ.

179
00:06:36.358 --> 00:06:38.279
The classroom is jarr, with kasra.

180
00:06:38.429 --> 00:06:40.980
It comes after a
preposition, the word for in.

181
00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:43.239
Four. They are in the mosque.

182
00:06:43.389 --> 00:06:45.724
‫هُمْ فِي المَسْجِدِ‬

183
00:06:46.074 --> 00:06:48.712
The word for they is the
Topic, in the place of rafʿ.

184
00:06:49.162 --> 00:06:51.032
Five. You two are in the house.

185
00:06:51.182 --> 00:06:53.351
‫أَنْتُمَا فِي البَيْتِ‬

186
00:06:53.701 --> 00:06:56.662
The word for you two is the
Topic, in the place of rafʿ.

187
00:06:57.112 --> 00:06:59.912
Six. Where is the boy?
He is in the mosque.

188
00:07:00.062 --> 00:07:03.624
‫أَيْنَ الوَلَدُ؟ هُوَ فِي المَسْجِدِ‬

189
00:07:03.974 --> 00:07:06.361
This one is from the
Madinah book, lesson four.

190
00:07:06.511 --> 00:07:08.116
The word for he is the Topic.

191
00:07:08.266 --> 00:07:09.545
It stands for the boy.

192
00:07:10.195 --> 00:07:12.981
One last tip. A pronoun
can replace a noun.

193
00:07:13.231 --> 00:07:15.056
The student is in the classroom.

194
00:07:15.206 --> 00:07:17.702
‫الطَّالِبُ فِي الفَصْلِ‬

195
00:07:18.052 --> 00:07:20.037
It becomes: He is in the classroom.

196
00:07:20.187 --> 00:07:22.016
‫هُوَ فِي الفَصْلِ‬

197
00:07:22.366 --> 00:07:24.413
Pick the pronoun by number and gender.

198
00:07:24.563 --> 00:07:26.636
One male student, so the word for he.

199
00:07:27.286 --> 00:07:28.138
In short.

200
00:07:28.388 --> 00:07:32.264
Fixed words are in every sentence.
Learn them once, as a table.

201
00:07:32.614 --> 00:07:34.553
There are twelve separate pronouns.

202
00:07:34.803 --> 00:07:35.636
‫أَنَا‬

203
00:07:35.786 --> 00:07:36.631
‫نَحْنُ‬

204
00:07:36.781 --> 00:07:37.610
‫أَنْتَ‬

205
00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:38.619
‫أَنْتِ‬

206
00:07:38.769 --> 00:07:39.776
‫أَنْتُمَا‬

207
00:07:39.926 --> 00:07:40.898
‫أَنْتُمْ‬

208
00:07:41.048 --> 00:07:42.302
‫أَنْتُنَّ‬

209
00:07:42.452 --> 00:07:43.273
‫هُوَ‬

210
00:07:43.423 --> 00:07:44.104
‫هِيَ‬

211
00:07:44.254 --> 00:07:45.045
‫هُمَا‬

212
00:07:45.195 --> 00:07:45.907
‫هُمْ‬

213
00:07:46.057 --> 00:07:46.885
‫هُنَّ‬

214
00:07:47.335 --> 00:07:50.049
Choose by person:
speaker, listener, absent.

215
00:07:50.199 --> 00:07:52.795
By number: one, two, more. And by gender.

216
00:07:53.145 --> 00:07:56.476
A pronoun never changes its
ending, but it still has a job.

217
00:07:56.826 --> 00:07:59.014
As the Topic, it is in the place of rafʿ.

218
00:07:59.264 --> 00:08:01.604
‫فِي مَحَلِّ رَفْعٍ‬

219
00:08:02.354 --> 00:08:04.988
Now it is your turn.
Open the Practice tab.

220
00:08:05.138 --> 00:08:06.830
There are six practice cards.

221
00:08:06.980 --> 00:08:10.537
Which pronoun? What does
it mean? Fixed or flexible?

222
00:08:10.787 --> 00:08:15.216
Replace the word with a pronoun.
Give the job, and rafʿ, naṣb or jarr.

223
00:08:15.216 --> 00:08:16.671
Then person and number.

224
00:08:16.921 --> 00:08:21.070
Then do the homework. And read the
table aloud, every day this week.
